{"id":"refine_20260929114737472","summary":"Saved a project-qualified global memory for Continual-ARC task task-68309966.","rationale":"The demonstrations and successful submission support a reusable stamping rule: preserve the template’s orientation and colors, and center it on each isolated marker. The task and project are explicitly named, making this a scoped, reusable lesson rather than a session-only note.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named task can apply the demonstrated template-copying rule; validate by checking that each marker receives the unchanged template centered on it and that the original template remains intact.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_68309966_stamp_the_template_on_isolated_markers","title":"Continual-ARC task-68309966: stamp the template on isolated markers","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-68309966, identify the large template against the uniform background and compute its tight bounding box. Copy the exact rectangle, preserving orientation and all cell colors, centered on each isolated color-1 marker; the marker aligns with the template's center cell. Preserve the original template. In the demonstrated instance, the 3×3 template is [[4,5,5],[8,5,8],[8,5,0]] against background 4, and its center cell is 5. Demos confirm that the template is copied as-is, including background-colored cells within its bounding rectangle.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-68309966"},"reason":"The demos establish the template-stamping transformation, and the successful submission confirms the centered placement and preservation of the original template.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_68309966_stamp_the_template_on_isolated_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-68309966: stamp the template on isolated markers","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-68309966, identify the large template against the uniform background and compute its tight bounding box. Copy the exact rectangle, preserving orientation and all cell colors, centered on each isolated color-1 marker; the marker aligns with the template's center cell. Preserve the original template. In the demonstrated instance, the 3×3 template is [[4,5,5],[8,5,8],[8,5,0]] against background 4, and its center cell is 5. Demos confirm that the template is copied as-is, including background-colored cells within its bounding rectangle.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-68309966"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:45.568Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:47:45.568Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929114841305","summary":"Saved the demonstrated template-matching rule for Continual-ARC task task-6f4d555a.","rationale":"A demo established that the marker’s shape is copied onto every translation whose corresponding cells are all background 0; the vertical-template test solve confirmed this rule, including overlapping matches.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named task can identify the marker offsets, scan for all-zero matches, recolor the union with the marker color, and preserve all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_6f4d555a_stamp_marker_template_on_zero_cells","title":"Continual-ARC task task-6f4d555a: stamp the marker template on zero cells","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-6f4d555a, treat the small non-background marker shape as a template. Find every translation where all corresponding cells in the grid are 0, then recolor the union of matched cells with the marker color. Preserve all other cells and the original marker; overlapping matches are allowed. Implementation hint: record the marker’s relative cell offsets, scan candidate anchors, require each target cell to be 0, then recolor those cells. Demo evidence: marker 6 formed a V at offsets (0,0), (1,-1), (1,1). Test evidence: marker 1 formed a vertical three-cell template, and recoloring every all-zero vertical triple produced a correct solve.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-6f4d555a"},"reason":"This is a stable, project-qualified task rule supported by a demo and a correct test solve.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_6f4d555a_stamp_marker_template_on_zero_cells","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-6f4d555a: stamp the marker template on zero cells","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-6f4d555a, treat the small non-background marker shape as a template. Find every translation where all corresponding cells in the grid are 0, then recolor the union of matched cells with the marker color. Preserve all other cells and the original marker; overlapping matches are allowed. Implementation hint: record the marker’s relative cell offsets, scan candidate anchors, require each target cell to be 0, then recolor those cells. Demo evidence: marker 6 formed a V at offsets (0,0), (1,-1), (1,1). Test evidence: marker 1 formed a vertical three-cell template, and recoloring every all-zero vertical triple produced a correct solve.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-6f4d555a"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:46.923Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:48:46.923Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115054399","summary":"Saved the confirmed fill rule for Continual-ARC task task-144828a7 as a global memory.","rationale":"The demos and correct test submission establish that every enclosed interior is filled with fixed color 4, regardless of outline color or interior size, while outlines and other cells remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named task can identify and fill all enclosed regions with color 4; validate by checking that no enclosed interior is missed and no outline or other cell is altered.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill all enclosed regions with 4","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of the outline color and interior size. Preserve the outlines and all other cells. The demos showed a color-3 outlined enclosure and multiple color-7 outlined rectangular enclosures; each interior was filled with 4. The test had two color-5 outlined enclosures; filling both interiors with 4 was confirmed correct. Color 4 is fixed, not derived from the outline color. Check for all closed interiors, not just one.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-144828a7"},"reason":"The task rule was supported by two demos and confirmed by a correct test submission.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill all enclosed regions with 4","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of the outline color and interior size. Preserve the outlines and all other cells. The demos showed a color-3 outlined enclosure and multiple color-7 outlined rectangular enclosures; each interior was filled with 4. The test had two color-5 outlined enclosures; filling both interiors with 4 was confirmed correct. Color 4 is fixed, not derived from the outline color. Check for all closed interiors, not just one.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-144828a7"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929115505949","summary":"Saved a cautious global memory that task-0c167358 remains unresolved and its apparent shape-matching rule is unconfirmed.","rationale":"The trajectory shows eight demos and eight unsuccessful attempts; several visually plausible recolorings were wrong, so the selection criterion should not be recorded as established.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named Continual-ARC task will avoid repeating unsupported recoloring guesses, use demonstrations to establish the criterion, and validate grid dimensions and cells before submission.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_0c167358_unresolved_shape_recoloring","title":"Continual-ARC task task-0c167358: shape-recoloring rule unresolved","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-0c167358, the rule remains unresolved despite eight demonstrations and eight unsuccessful attempts. Do not assume that a duplicate-looking polyomino should be recolored to the color of a prominent line- or L-shaped object. In the observed test, recoloring the lower-right color-8 component to 2, 4, or 0 was incorrect; recoloring the color-0 pattern or upper color-3 L to 2 was also incorrect. Demonstrations often changed one non-background component to the color of a prominent line/L-shaped object, but the selection criterion was not established. On future instances, use demonstrations to determine the actual matching criterion, carefully verify every row and cell, and treat visual resemblance as a hypothesis rather than a confirmed rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-0c167358","confidence":"cautious; unresolved"},"reason":"Preserves the explicit requested warning and the demonstrated failure outcomes without promoting an unsupported rule.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_0c167358_unresolved_shape_recoloring","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-0c167358: shape-recoloring rule unresolved","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-0c167358, the rule remains unresolved despite eight demonstrations and eight unsuccessful attempts. Do not assume that a duplicate-looking polyomino should be recolored to the color of a prominent line- or L-shaped object. In the observed test, recoloring the lower-right color-8 component to 2, 4, or 0 was incorrect; recoloring the color-0 pattern or upper color-3 L to 2 was also incorrect. Demonstrations often changed one non-background component to the color of a prominent line/L-shaped object, but the selection criterion was not established. On future instances, use demonstrations to determine the actual matching criterion, carefully verify every row and cell, and treat visual resemblance as a hypothesis rather than a confirmed rule.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-0c167358","confidence":"cautious; unresolved"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:55:10.861Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:55:10.861Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120046804","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task task-144828a7 with the solved edge-enclosure case and validated cautions.","rationale":"The successful instance and demonstrations show that a background region can be enclosed by outline cells together with a grid edge, while other boundary-touching or corner regions may remain open. Multiple plausible but incorrect fills confirm that candidate regions must be traced individually.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should fill only genuinely enclosed regions with 4, preserve outlines and all other cells, and distinguish edge-closed pockets from open or exterior regions.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. A region may be enclosed by three sides of the outline plus one grid edge; do not treat every background component touching the grid boundary as exterior. Conversely, a region at a grid corner or touching two grid edges is not automatically fillable: trace its boundaries and determine whether the outline actually closes it. In the solved 20x25 instance, the only fill was rows 5–8, columns 22–24 (0-indexed); other edge-adjacent regions remained unchanged. Failed guesses included leaving the grid unchanged, filling both right-side pockets, filling only the bottom-right pocket, filling all but the largest component, and filling every region. For future instances, trace each candidate pocket individually, verify that its outline-and-edge boundary closes it, then change only its interior cells to 4.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserves the confirmed task rule while adding the demonstrated edge-enclosure nuance and warnings against unsupported blanket fill strategies.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill all enclosed regions with 4","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of the outline color and interior size. Preserve the outlines and all other cells. The demos showed a color-3 outlined enclosure and multiple color-7 outlined rectangular enclosures; each interior was filled with 4. The test had two color-5 outlined enclosures; filling both interiors with 4 was confirmed correct. Color 4 is fixed, not derived from the outline color. Check for all closed interiors, not just one.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-144828a7"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. A region may be enclosed by three sides of the outline plus one grid edge; do not treat every background component touching the grid boundary as exterior. Conversely, a region at a grid corner or touching two grid edges is not automatically fillable: trace its boundaries and determine whether the outline actually closes it. In the solved 20x25 instance, the only fill was rows 5–8, columns 22–24 (0-indexed); other edge-adjacent regions remained unchanged. Failed guesses included leaving the grid unchanged, filling both right-side pockets, filling only the bottom-right pocket, filling all but the largest component, and filling every region. For future instances, trace each candidate pocket individually, verify that its outline-and-edge boundary closes it, then change only its interior cells to 4.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:00:52.151Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120102482","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task-144828a7 with another confirmed successful enclosure-fill instance.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms that a closed 7-colored rectangle enclosing a 3×3 region of color 5 should have only its interior changed to 4; vertical outline extensions and all exterior cells remain unchanged.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named task can apply the enclosed-region rule while preserving outlines and exterior cells; validate by checking that only fully enclosed interior cells change to 4.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four (general, v3)","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color, background color, and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. Enclosure may be formed by a closed outline, including a pocket adjacent to the grid edge when the outline genuinely closes it; do not fill open or exterior regions. Confirmed instance: a 7-colored closed rectangular outline around a 3×3 region of color 5, with vertical line extensions above and below, required changing only the nine interior cells to 4. The successful output preserved the outline, extensions, and all exterior cells.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Persist an additional zero-error confirmation and clarify preservation of outline extensions and exterior cells.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. A region may be enclosed by three sides of the outline plus one grid edge; do not treat every background component touching the grid boundary as exterior. Conversely, a region at a grid corner or touching two grid edges is not automatically fillable: trace its boundaries and determine whether the outline actually closes it. In the solved 20x25 instance, the only fill was rows 5–8, columns 22–24 (0-indexed); other edge-adjacent regions remained unchanged. Failed guesses included leaving the grid unchanged, filling both right-side pockets, filling only the bottom-right pocket, filling all but the largest component, and filling every region. For future instances, trace each candidate pocket individually, verify that its outline-and-edge boundary closes it, then change only its interior cells to 4.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:00:52.151Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four (general, v3)","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color, background color, and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. Enclosure may be formed by a closed outline, including a pocket adjacent to the grid edge when the outline genuinely closes it; do not fill open or exterior regions. Confirmed instance: a 7-colored closed rectangular outline around a 3×3 region of color 5, with vertical line extensions above and below, required changing only the nine interior cells to 4. The successful output preserved the outline, extensions, and all exterior cells.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:06.716Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120243546","summary":"Updated the global task-144828a7 memory with another correct enclosure-fill validation.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms the existing rule on a fresh 17x14 grid: exactly two enclosed background regions were filled, while exterior cells, outline cells, and protruding arms were preserved.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should continue to fill only genuinely enclosed regions with 4, regardless of dimensions or colors; validate that open and exterior areas and all outline cells remain unchanged.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every genuinely enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color, background color, or interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells; do not fill open or exterior regions. Confirmed on a 17x14 grid with background 3 and outline 6: the two enclosed pockets at zero-based rows 4–5, columns 3–7, and rows 11–12, columns 3–5, were filled with 4. Protruding outline arms and exterior background were preserved.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a new zero-error validation for the existing project-qualified rule, including the locations of both enclosed pockets and the preservation constraints.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four (general, v3)","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every fully enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color, background color, and interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells. Enclosure may be formed by a closed outline, including a pocket adjacent to the grid edge when the outline genuinely closes it; do not fill open or exterior regions. Confirmed instance: a 7-colored closed rectangular outline around a 3×3 region of color 5, with vertical line extensions above and below, required changing only the nine interior cells to 4. The successful output preserved the outline, extensions, and all exterior cells.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:06.716Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_144828a7_fill_enclosed_regions_with_four","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-144828a7: fill enclosed regions with four","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-144828a7, fill every genuinely enclosed interior region with color 4, independent of outline color, background color, or interior size. Preserve outline cells and all other cells; do not fill open or exterior regions. Confirmed on a 17x14 grid with background 3 and outline 6: the two enclosed pockets at zero-based rows 4–5, columns 3–7, and rows 11–12, columns 3–5, were filled with 4. Protruding outline arms and exterior background were preserved.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T11:50:59.908Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:02:47.776Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120350511","summary":"Saved the validated panel-counting rule for Continual-ARC task task-268b9b65 as a global memory.","rationale":"Two demonstrations and the correctly submitted test support counting marker cells independently in each panel and mapping the count to one output cell.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this named task can produce the panel summary; validate by identifying separator-bounded panels, counting markers in each, and preserving panel order.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_268b9b65_count_markers_in_panels","title":"Continual-ARC task task-268b9b65: count markers in panels","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-268b9b65, divide the grid at full separator lines into rectangular panels. Count the isolated marker cells in each panel, excluding separators. Output one cell per panel in the same row/column order: if a panel contains exactly one marker, output the background color; if it contains two markers, output color 1. Demonstrations used marker 9 on background 2 with separator color 7, and marker 4 on background 9 with separator color 6. The test used marker 5 on background 6 with separator color 3; panel counts [[2,1,2],[1,2,1],[2,2,2]] correctly produced [[1,6,1],[6,1,6],[1,1,1]].","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-268b9b65"},"reason":"The mapping was supported by two demonstrations and a correctly accepted test submission.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_268b9b65_count_markers_in_panels","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task task-268b9b65: count markers in panels","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-268b9b65, divide the grid at full separator lines into rectangular panels. Count the isolated marker cells in each panel, excluding separators. Output one cell per panel in the same row/column order: if a panel contains exactly one marker, output the background color; if it contains two markers, output color 1. Demonstrations used marker 9 on background 2 with separator color 7, and marker 4 on background 9 with separator color 6. The test used marker 5 on background 6 with separator color 3; panel counts [[2,1,2],[1,2,1],[2,2,2]] correctly produced [[1,6,1],[6,1,6],[1,1,1]].","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-268b9b65"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:03:55.293Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:03:55.293Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929120638269","summary":"Saved the validated Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132 rule and the correction that rays stop at the marker.","rationale":"The task was solved after one incorrect submission, and the demos plus test output support the bar-and-marker projection rule and the specific ray endpoint correction.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-b2cb1132 can apply the projection and recoloring rule while preserving bars and unrelated cells; validate by checking each marker’s ray direction, endpoint, and corresponding projection from the opposite bar.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_b2cb1132_project_marker_rays_between_border_bars","title":"Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132: project marker rays between border bars","content":"For Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132, identify the uniform background, two equal-length special-color bars on opposite borders, and sparse marker cells. Preserve both bars and unrelated background. Recolor each marker to 4. Draw from each marker a straight ray in its original marker color toward the aligned border bar, filling only the cells between marker and bar; do not extend past the marker. Also project marker positions along their bar span to the opposite bar: at each corresponding offset, draw an inward ray from that opposite bar using the marker color. In the solved 10x6 example, background 6; color-5 bars at left rows 0–3 and right rows 6–9; color-2 markers at (6,1),(7,2),(8,1),(9,1). Rows 0–3 fill columns 1–5 with 2. In rows 6–9, fill from each marker rightward through column 4 with 2, changing the marker to 4; row 7 column 1 remains 6. The initial wrong attempt extended that row’s ray past its marker, so carefully preserve the direction and stop at the marker.","path":"continual-arc","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-b2cb1132"},"reason":"This named task’s rule was validated by the correct submission, and recording the endpoint correction directly addresses the demonstrated error.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_b2cb1132_project_marker_rays_between_border_bars","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132: project marker rays between border bars","content":"For Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132, identify the uniform background, two equal-length special-color bars on opposite borders, and sparse marker cells. Preserve both bars and unrelated background. Recolor each marker to 4. Draw from each marker a straight ray in its original marker color toward the aligned border bar, filling only the cells between marker and bar; do not extend past the marker. Also project marker positions along their bar span to the opposite bar: at each corresponding offset, draw an inward ray from that opposite bar using the marker color. In the solved 10x6 example, background 6; color-5 bars at left rows 0–3 and right rows 6–9; color-2 markers at (6,1),(7,2),(8,1),(9,1). Rows 0–3 fill columns 1–5 with 2. In rows 6–9, fill from each marker rightward through column 4 with 2, changing the marker to 4; row 7 column 1 remains 6. The initial wrong attempt extended that row’s ray past its marker, so carefully preserve the direction and stop at the marker.","path":"continual-arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-b2cb1132"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:45.660Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:45.660Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
