{"id":"refine_20260929123425548","summary":"Updated the global memory for Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132 with the corrected, validated paired-ray rule.","rationale":"The successful submission confirms that marker offsets activate paired cells on the opposing border bars, with one ray ending at the marker and the paired ray extending to the far edge. The two earlier submissions failed by projecting indiscriminately or filling both directions in the marker’s column.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should activate only offsets indicated by markers, preserve bars and unrelated cells, recolor each marker to 4, and correctly include the far-edge interior cell on the paired ray. Validate bar-offset pairing, ray direction and endpoints, dimensions, and untouched cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_b2cb1132_project_marker_rays_between_border_bars","title":"Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132: project marker rays between paired border bars (validated)","content":"For Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132, identify the uniform background, two equal-length color-6 bars on opposing borders, and sparse color-9 markers. Pair bar cells by their offset along the bars. A marker on a perpendicular ray from one bar activates that offset pair: draw color 9 from the marker-side bar cell to the marker, recolor the marker to 4, and draw color 9 from the paired cell on the opposite bar all the way to the far edge, including the far-edge interior cell. Preserve both bars and every unrelated/background cell. In a validated 20x19 instance, the top bar occupied columns 9–17 and the bottom bar columns 0–8, so top column 9+k paired with bottom column k. Markers at (row,column) (4,14), (7,17), (9,16), (14,13), and (17,12) activated offsets k=5,8,7,4,3. Their top-side rays filled columns 14,17,16,13,12 from row 1 through each marker; paired bottom-side rays filled columns 5,8,7,4,3 from row 0 through row 18; each marker became 4. Do not project every bar cell without a marker, and do not fill both directions in the marker’s own column. Validate dimensions, paired offsets, ray directions/endpoints, and preservation of untouched cells.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","validation":"successful submission after two incorrect projections"},"reason":"A fresh solved instance established the exact offset pairing and ray endpoints, resolving ambiguity in the previous projection description.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_b2cb1132_project_marker_rays_between_border_bars","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132: project marker rays between border bars (validated)","content":"For Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132, identify the uniform background, two equal-length special-color bars on opposite borders, and sparse marker cells. For each marker, use its offset along the border bar to project the marker’s original color inward along the perpendicular axis from the corresponding bar position, stopping at the marker; change the marker to 4. Also project that color inward from the corresponding offset on the opposite bar toward the far border, including the far boundary cell while preserving the bar cells. Match offsets in the same left-to-right or top-to-bottom order on both bars. Preserve all unrelated cells. Confirmed 22×18 case: background 9; top bar color 0 at row 0, columns 3–4; bottom bar at row 21, columns 16–17; marker color 1 at (5,3). Output retains both full bars, colors column 3 rows 1–4 with 1, changes (5,3) to 4, and colors column 16 rows 0–20 with 1. Prior failed guesses omitted the top bar’s second cell; retain it. Demos confirm that rays use the marker’s original color and markers become 4.","path":"continual-arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-b2cb1132","validation":"Correct submission on a fresh instance; consistent with demonstrated examples"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:45.660Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:19:07.336Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_b2cb1132_project_marker_rays_between_border_bars","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132: project marker rays between paired border bars (validated)","content":"For Continual-ARC task-b2cb1132, identify the uniform background, two equal-length color-6 bars on opposing borders, and sparse color-9 markers. Pair bar cells by their offset along the bars. A marker on a perpendicular ray from one bar activates that offset pair: draw color 9 from the marker-side bar cell to the marker, recolor the marker to 4, and draw color 9 from the paired cell on the opposite bar all the way to the far edge, including the far-edge interior cell. Preserve both bars and every unrelated/background cell. In a validated 20x19 instance, the top bar occupied columns 9–17 and the bottom bar columns 0–8, so top column 9+k paired with bottom column k. Markers at (row,column) (4,14), (7,17), (9,16), (14,13), and (17,12) activated offsets k=5,8,7,4,3. Their top-side rays filled columns 14,17,16,13,12 from row 1 through each marker; paired bottom-side rays filled columns 5,8,7,4,3 from row 0 through row 18; each marker became 4. Do not project every bar cell without a marker, and do not fill both directions in the marker’s own column. Validate dimensions, paired offsets, ray directions/endpoints, and preservation of untouched cells.","path":"continual-arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","validation":"successful submission after two incorrect projections"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:06:45.660Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:34:33.392Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929125433018","summary":"Created a global memory for Continual-ARC task-7017344c’s validated template-stamping rule.","rationale":"One demonstration and the successfully solved test support copying the template unchanged at each isolated marker, aligned using the task’s demonstrated marker-to-template offset. The first incorrect attempt also shows the value of checking every stamp’s full footprint.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can preserve the original template, stamp a correctly aligned copy at every marker, and verify all copied cells and unchanged background before submission.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_7017344c_stamp_template_at_markers","title":"Continual-ARC task-7017344c: stamp template at isolated markers","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-7017344c, identify the multicolor template and isolated marker cells. Copy the exact template, preserving orientation and all colors, at each marker using the marker-to-template alignment established by the example; preserve the original template and all unrelated cells. The demonstration used a 5×3 template and isolated 0 markers, with each stamp’s top-left positioned so the marker was offset (2,1) from that corner. A fresh test used the vertical template [7,1,7,7,7] and isolated 8 markers; the validated stamps placed the marker row at template offset (1,0). Determine the alignment from the instance’s template/marker arrangement rather than assuming one fixed offset across different template layouts. Check every stamp’s complete footprint, including its topmost and bottommost cells, before submitting.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-7017344c","evidence":"One demonstration pair and a successful test solve; first submission was incorrect."},"reason":"Preserves the demonstrated transformation and a concrete validation lesson for future instances of this recurring task.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_7017344c_stamp_template_at_markers","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-7017344c: stamp template at isolated markers","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-7017344c, identify the multicolor template and isolated marker cells. Copy the exact template, preserving orientation and all colors, at each marker using the marker-to-template alignment established by the example; preserve the original template and all unrelated cells. The demonstration used a 5×3 template and isolated 0 markers, with each stamp’s top-left positioned so the marker was offset (2,1) from that corner. A fresh test used the vertical template [7,1,7,7,7] and isolated 8 markers; the validated stamps placed the marker row at template offset (1,0). Determine the alignment from the instance’s template/marker arrangement rather than assuming one fixed offset across different template layouts. Check every stamp’s complete footprint, including its topmost and bottommost cells, before submitting.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-7017344c","evidence":"One demonstration pair and a successful test solve; first submission was incorrect."},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:54:42.417Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:54:42.417Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929125807682","summary":"Saved the validated Continual-ARC task-dbda802d lattice-to-color-map rule as a global memory.","rationale":"Seven demonstrations and the correctly solved test support mapping each region to its shared non-background corner-marker color, otherwise to the interior background, then trimming trailing background-only rows and columns. Earlier untrimmed submissions were incorrect.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of task-dbda802d can construct the region map and trim it before submission; validate corner colors, background fallback, and output bounds against the examples.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: map lattice corner markers and trim background","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-dbda802d, identify the regularly spaced horizontal and vertical separator lines and the uniform interior/background color. Each output cell corresponds to a region between adjacent horizontal and vertical separators. Inspect the four marker/intersection cells at that region's corners: if all four have the same non-background color, output that color; otherwise output the interior/background color. After forming the map, trim trailing rows and columns that are entirely background, respecting the valid grid bounds. Do not submit the untrimmed map. Validated across seven demonstrations and the test instance: the raw map [6,3,3] trimmed to [[6]], which was accepted.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"seven demonstrations and correctly solved test"},"reason":"Preserves the demonstrated transformation and the crucial trimming step that corrected earlier incorrect submissions.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: map lattice corner markers and trim background","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-dbda802d, identify the regularly spaced horizontal and vertical separator lines and the uniform interior/background color. Each output cell corresponds to a region between adjacent horizontal and vertical separators. Inspect the four marker/intersection cells at that region's corners: if all four have the same non-background color, output that color; otherwise output the interior/background color. After forming the map, trim trailing rows and columns that are entirely background, respecting the valid grid bounds. Do not submit the untrimmed map. Validated across seven demonstrations and the test instance: the raw map [6,3,3] trimmed to [[6]], which was accepted.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"seven demonstrations and correctly solved test"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929130251882","summary":"Saved the validated Continual-ARC task-4342a43e pattern-selection rule as a global memory.","rationale":"The solved test and demonstrations support using the large L marker’s color to recolor the matching copy on the side opposite its horizontal arm; earlier submissions incorrectly targeted unrelated dominoes.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can identify the large L, find congruent copies, and recolor the correctly positioned copy; validate the marker arms, copy placement, and preservation of all other cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_4342a43e_select_copy_opposite_l_arm","title":"Continual-ARC task-4342a43e: recolor the matching copy opposite the large L arm","content":"For Continual-ARC task-4342a43e, identify the large L-shaped marker and use its color as the recoloring color. Find congruent object-pattern copies and select the copy on the side opposite the L's horizontal arm, relative to its vertical stem. Recolor only that matched copy; preserve the marker, other copies, and all unrelated cells. Distinguish the large L marker from smaller markers. Demonstrations include changing a target of another color and choosing between duplicated same-color shapes. Validate the L arm directions, the selected copy's position, and exact changed cells; avoid targeting unrelated dominoes or markers.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-4342a43e"},"reason":"The successful test and multiple demonstrations establish a recurring, task-specific selection and recoloring rule.","after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_4342a43e_select_copy_opposite_l_arm","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-4342a43e: recolor the matching copy opposite the large L arm","content":"For Continual-ARC task-4342a43e, identify the large L-shaped marker and use its color as the recoloring color. Find congruent object-pattern copies and select the copy on the side opposite the