{"id":"refine_20260929131633048","summary":"Updated the global task-fb46062c memory with a fresh successful validation.","rationale":"The 2×1 uniform input filled with color 2 produced a correct 6×2 uniform output with zero wrong submissions, confirming the 3H×2W dimensions and preservation of uniform values.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can apply the confirmed dimension rule and preserve uniform grids; validate output dimensions and cell values.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_fb46062c_3h_2w_output_uniform_grids_preserved","title":"Continual-ARC task-fb46062c: 3H×2W output; uniform grids preserved","content":"For Continual-ARC task-fb46062c, the output dimensions are 3H×2W. A fresh test input of size 2×1, uniformly filled with color 2, was correctly transformed into a uniform 6×2 grid of color 2 with zero wrong submissions. This confirms that uniform input values are preserved across the output. Demonstrations also support the 3H×2W dimension rule; check dimensions and preserve cell values, especially for uniform inputs.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Record the fresh successful test validation in the existing project-qualified memory.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_fb46062c_3h_2w_output_uniform_grids_preserved","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-fb46062c: 3H×2W output; uniform grids preserved","content":"For task-fb46062c, the validated test instance was a 2×3 grid filled with color 2. Correct output was a 6×6 grid filled with color 2 (zero wrong attempts). Demonstrations show output dimensions are 3H×2W. One 1×5 demo [0,6,3,4,0] produced three identical rows [0,4,3,6,0,0,6,3,4,0], i.e. horizontal reversal concatenated with the input. An 8×6 demo also produced 24×12 but its pattern is more involved, so do not assume the simple concat/repeat rule for arbitrary nonuniform grids without further evidence. For all-uniform inputs, preserve the sole color in every output cell and scale dimensions to 3H×2W.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:03:47.897837+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:03:47.897854+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_fb46062c_3h_2w_output_uniform_grids_preserved","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-fb46062c: 3H×2W output; uniform grids preserved","content":"For Continual-ARC task-fb46062c, the output dimensions are 3H×2W. A fresh test input of size 2×1, uniformly filled with color 2, was correctly transformed into a uniform 6×2 grid of color 2 with zero wrong submissions. This confirms that uniform input values are preserved across the output. Demonstrations also support the 3H×2W dimension rule; check dimensions and preserve cell values, especially for uniform inputs.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:03:47.897837+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:16:37.265Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929132303848","summary":"Updated the global task-dbda802d memory with the validated panel-map rule and corrected the earlier mistaken interpretation.","rationale":"The task was solved correctly after a demo clarified that repeated special-color markers at divider intersections encode panel cells, while the repeated panel-interior color supplies the default. The user explicitly requested updating the existing global memory.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should construct the compressed panel map, overlay cells encoded by matching 2×2 divider-intersection markers, and trim rows or columns containing only the default color; validate dimensions and cell placement against examples.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: encode divider markers as panel colors and trim default background","content":"For Continual-ARC task-dbda802d, treat the input as a lattice of uniform panels separated by divider lines. The repeated panel-interior color is the default output color (for example, 2 in the validated test and 8 in the demo). A special color appearing at all four intersections formed by adjacent horizontal and vertical dividers—a 2×2 block of same-color intersection markers—encodes that color in the corresponding single panel cell. Build the compressed panel map at panel resolution, initialize it with the default color, and overlay each encoded special color in its corresponding cell. Then trim outer rows and columns containing only the default color. Do not treat divider-intersection markers as output pixels or simply copy them into a lattice map. Validated test output: [[2,2,2,7],[6,2,2,2],[2,2,2,2],[2,1,2,8]]. A separate demo validated a trimmed 6×3 output.","metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"correct submission and one demo"},"reason":"Replace the earlier incomplete lattice-map description with the precise rule established by the demo and correct test submission, including the default color, marker encoding, trimming, and a warning against the failed interpretation.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: corner-marker region map with tight background trim (validated)","content":"For Continual-ARC task task-dbda802d, find the regular horizontal and vertical separator lines and the interior fill color. Each output cell corresponds to one rectangular region between adjacent horizontal and adjacent vertical lines. Read the four marker values at the region's corner intersections: if all four are the same color and that color is neither the separator-line color nor the interior fill, output that color; otherwise output the interior fill. Color 0 is a valid marker color when it differs from the interior fill and separator color. After forming the map, trim background-only rows and columns from all edges to the tight bounding box of non-background output cells; leading blank rows/columns can matter, so do not only trim the trailing edges. Fresh validation: on the 22x27 instance with interior 7, separator 4, marker intersections at rows 0,3,6,9,12,15,18,21 and columns 2,8,14,20,26, the correct trimmed result was [[7,7,0,0],[5,7,7,7],[5,5,7,9],[7,5,7,9],[7,5,7,9]]. Carefully read all marker intersections, including row 15/18 column 8, which were 5. The rule was consistent with eight requested demos.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"validated on current fresh test and eight demonstrations"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:16:21.905576+00:00","version":2},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: encode divider markers as panel colors and trim default background","content":"For Continual-ARC task-dbda802d, treat the input as a lattice of uniform panels separated by divider lines. The repeated panel-interior color is the default output color (for example, 2 in the validated test and 8 in the demo). A special color appearing at all four intersections formed by adjacent horizontal and vertical dividers—a 2×2 block of same-color intersection markers—encodes that color in the corresponding single panel cell. Build the compressed panel map at panel resolution, initialize it with the default color, and overlay each encoded special color in its corresponding cell. Then trim outer rows and columns containing only the default color. Do not treat divider-intersection markers as output pixels or simply copy them into a lattice map. Validated test output: [[2,2,2,7],[6,2,2,2],[2,2,2,2],[2,1,2,8]]. A separate demo validated a trimmed 6×3 output.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"correct submission and one demo"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:12.974Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929132644381","summary":"Updated the global task-dbda802d memory with the fresh validated output and the correction to preserve internal default cells.","rationale":"This instance confirmed the lattice-to-map rule and exposed a prior mistake: removing internal all-default columns changes the map’s spacing; only outer margins should be cropped.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should map matching adjacent 2×2 intersection blocks onto the panel-color map, retain internal default cells, and crop only to the tight outer bounds of encoded non-default cells.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: encode divider markers as panel colors and trim default background (general, v4)","content":"For Continual-ARC task-dbda802d, treat the grid as uniform panels separated by divider rows and columns. Identify the divider-line background color and the uniform interior panel color. Read the intersection cells of the divider lines as a marker matrix. For each adjacent 2×2 block of intersections, if all four values are the same color and that color differs from the divider-line background, write that color into the corresponding output-map cell. Initialize map cells with the uniform panel-interior color. Crop the map to the tight bounding box of encoded non-default cells, but retain internal all-default rows and columns; do not compress away internal spacing. An unmarked block of divider-background intersections does not encode an output color. Fresh validation: crossing rows [0,8,16], crossing columns [2,5,8,11,14,17,20,23], panel fill 9, and divider background 2 produced [[5,9,9,9,3],[9,9,5,9,9]], confirmed correct.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds a fresh successful validation and corrects the demonstrated error of deleting internal default columns.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: encode divider markers as panel colors and trim default background","content":"For Continual-ARC task-dbda802d, treat the input as a lattice of uniform panels separated by divider lines. The repeated panel-interior color is the default output color (for example, 2 in the validated test and 8 in the demo). A special color appearing at all four intersections formed by adjacent horizontal and vertical dividers—a 2×2 block of same-color intersection markers—encodes that color in the corresponding single panel cell. Build the compressed panel map at panel resolution, initialize it with the default color, and overlay each encoded special color in its corresponding cell. Then trim outer rows and columns containing only the default color. Do not treat divider-intersection markers as output pixels or simply copy them into a lattice map. Validated test output: [[2,2,2,7],[6,2,2,2],[2,2,2,2],[2,1,2,8]]. A separate demo validated a trimmed 6×3 output.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","project":"Continual-ARC","task_id":"task-dbda802d","validation":"correct submission and one demo"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:23:12.974Z","version":3},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_dbda802d_lattice_marker_map_trim_background","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-dbda802d: encode divider markers as panel colors and trim default background (general, v4)","content":"For Continual-ARC task-dbda802d, treat the grid as uniform panels separated by divider rows and columns. Identify the divider-line background color and the uniform interior panel color. Read the intersection cells of the divider lines as a marker matrix. For each adjacent 2×2 block of intersections, if all four values are the same color and that color differs from the divider-line background, write that color into the corresponding output-map cell. Initialize map cells with the uniform panel-interior color. Crop the map to the tight bounding box of encoded non-default cells, but retain internal all-default rows and columns; do not compress away internal spacing. An unmarked block of divider-background intersections does not encode an output color. Fresh validation: crossing rows [0,8,16], crossing columns [2,5,8,11,14,17,20,23], panel fill 9, and divider background 2 produced [[5,9,9,9,3],[9,9,5,9,9]], confirmed correct.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:58:14.527Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:26:52.405Z","version":4},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
