54be068, the grid contains multiple solid rectangular objects of different colors on a uniform background, with scattered single-cell color noise and occasional corrupted cells inside rectangles. Detect each intended rectangle from its color arrangement/bounding box, restore it as a solid rectangle in that same color, and replace stray noise outside the rectangles with the background color. Do not assume only one foreground color: preserve all sizeable rectangular objects, including small 2×2 blocks and rectangles of other colors (e.g. 9 in the solved instance), as well as larger blocks. Demo 1 showed 5 rectangles normalized and isolated 6/7/0 speckles removed; demo 2 confirmed several rectangle colors (5, 7, 3, 0), noise removal, and preserving distinct rectangles. Solved fresh test after initially erasing valid 9 rectangles: corrected rule was to keep all rectangle objects, not just the dominant color.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"task_id":"task-554be068","version":1,"evidence":"2 demos + successful test after 1 incorrect submission"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:47:54.333033+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:47:54.333050+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"continual_arc_task_554be068_restore_colored_rectangles_and_remove_speckles","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-554be068: restore colored rectangles and remove speckles","content":"For Continual-ARC task-554be068, identify the uniform background and each intended solid, axis-aligned colored rectangle. Restore every cell within each rectangle's full bounds to its rectangle color, including cells corrupted by noise; replace isolated noise outside rectangles with the background. Freshly validated on a 19x13 instance with background color 3: rectangles (inclusive, zero-based bounds) were color 4 at rows 0–4, cols 0–2; color 4 at rows 2–7, cols 5–8; color 4 at rows 10–16, cols 4–6; color 1 at rows 1–6, cols 10–11; color 5 at rows 9–11, cols 8–9; and color 8 at rows 13–18, cols 10–11. Isolated noise of colors 2 and 9 was replaced with background. An initial answer incorrectly ended the upper-middle color-4 rectangle at row 6; the accepted answer extended it through row 7. Carefully verify rectangle terminal rows and columns before submitting.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:47:54.333033+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:48:46.855Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
