ion: hollow frames of colors 1 and 4 and a 3×3 patch of color 5 had their enclosed interiors filled with 7; borders remained unchanged. A fresh test with a hollow color-5 frame and a color-9 3×3 patch missing its center was solved by filling the frame interior and patch center with 7, with zero wrong submissions.","path":"continual_arc","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:49:57.876Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:49:57.876Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682218/attempts/f6c94624865c4ccda9316988da8a6b85/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20260929135141779","summary":"Updated the global task-bb5337bf memory with the validated cellwise overlap rule and a warning against using only the first panel.","rationale":"The demonstrations and solved test confirm that the output marks corresponding cells where both panels contain color 2, regardless of whether the separator is vertical or horizontal. Transforming the first panel alone was tried and failed.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances should produce a panel-sized output with color 3 exactly at aligned 2-and-2 overlaps and color 2 elsewhere; validate panel orientation, dimensions, and every marked coordinate.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"continual_arc_task_bb5337bf_compare_two_panels_and_highlight_matching_cells","title":"Continual-ARC task-bb5337bf: highlight aligned color-2 overlaps","content":"For Continual-ARC task-bb5337bf, split the input into two equal-sized panels at the full solid separator row or column, excluding the separator. Align corresponding cells without flipping or rotating. Output one panel's dimensions, filled with color 2; place color 3 exactly where both panels contain color 2, and leave all other positions color 2. This rule applies whether the separator is vertical or horizontal. A transformation based only on color-2 cells in the first panel was tested and failed; the overlap condition is essential. Validate output dimensions and the coordinate-by-coordinate intersection before submission.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The rule was confirmed by a demonstration and a correctly solved test instance in both separator orientations.","before":{"id":"continual_arc_task_bb5337bf_compare_two_panels_and_highlight_matching_cells","kind":"memory","title":"Continual-ARC task-bb5337bf: compare two panels and highlight matching cells","content":"For task-bb5337bf, the input has two equal-sized panels separated by a full solid line (separator may be vertical or horizontal). Remove the separ